div.p:

	adripuimus
, caught; 
	hausimus
, imbibed; expressimus, wrought out; 
	imbuti
, steeped.


	imaginibus
 (cf. formas, 1.28), waxen masks of ancestors, worn by persons in the funeral procession, to represent the departed worthies (see note on the jus imaginum, Introduction, p.1, N.1); 
	cantu
, music; ludis, games; 
	exsequiis
, procession; 
	funere
, burial rites.
